mls — third-party attribution
=============================

Everything third-party in this module comes from one place, the IETF, and two
written grants cover all of it. Both are in BCP 78 / the IETF Trust Legal
Provisions 5.0. Nothing here rests on an argument about what is or is not
copyrightable; that reasoning was removed on 2026-09-09 once the grants were
read, and it is in this file's git history if it is ever wanted back.

1. THE 15 JSON FILES under `src/data/` are the MLS working group's interop
   test vectors, taken from https://github.com/mlswg/mls-implementations at
   commit `cfd450286d1bfd9cd2519b95c80f9771f94a5b1a` (2026-04-22). Nine are
   redistributed in full and without modification; five keep a subset of the
   upstream records, every retained record unmodified; `tree-operations.json`
   holds all five of its upstream records unmodified but re-serialised, so its
   bytes differ while its content does not.

   These files were contributed to an IETF working group, which makes them
   IETF Contributions (RFC 5378 §1.a), and TLP 5.0 §3.a grants anyone the
   right to copy, publish, display and distribute them — in full under
   §3.a(i), as unmodified portions under §3.a(iii). §3.a(iii)(x) asks for
   attribution in return, and this paragraph is it: the material is taken from
   IETF Contributions to the IETF MLS working group, published at the URL and
   commit named above.

   The upstream repository carries no LICENSE file of its own. That does not
   decide anything here — the grant follows from what the contributors did,
   not from what the repository posted.

